    "articleBody": " Midwest Images  When it comes to decorating and renovating your workplace, there are many ideas that come to mind, whereas some people are creative in their own ways and some like to take the reference from the internet or Pinterest. However, if you are looking to go for renovation or redecorating with a DIY bubble tube, there are many things that require your special attention before you begin with your very first project of DIY bubble walls.  Here are some of the tips to help you design the perfect DIY bubble wall and that too without too much hassle.   \tInstalling the DIY indoor bubble wall set up  There are many important aspects of installing DIY indoor fountain, and that involves the professional touch of installation. But before you begin to install the DIY indoor water feature you need to build a support frame for the wall that provides the strength and support system.  If you aren't good enough at building up the frame, it is advisable to go for the ready-to-install frames that are available in the market.  However, one of the most important things to take note of to build DIY indoor wall fountains is the firm support of the frame to ensure that the whole weight is rested on the bottom of the setup.   \tFixing of the unit in aligned position  Here it is important to note that when you are designing a DIY indoor water wall, you need to make sure that the wall unit is perfectly aligned to the wall and is placed on the appropriate position to avoid any imbalance and spillage of water from the bottom of the unit.  Whereas, it is also essential to take note that the position of the unit that you have placed is in a way that it can easily produce continuous bubbles from the output of the bubble jet.  Thus, it should be kept in mind that the complete and efficient working of the water wall and the bubbling fountain is dependent on the placement of the whole unit, and therefore, special attention should be needed to fixing the unit to the wall with all the energy and concentration.  One of the essential things to note is that one should also make sure that when you are placing the DIY indoor water feature at your workplace, or restaurant, the position of the unit should be accessible enough to make sure that you are able to maintain the unit from time to time.   \tMaintenance and cleanliness of the DIY indoor water wall  These acrylic water walls that you have invested in are going to be a long term part of your workplace so you are able to work upon its cleanliness and maintenance, and therefore, you should take care of the water wall by changing the water of the wall after every 4 to 6 weeks keeping sure that the water inside the bubble wall doesn't turn pale or yellow.  Moreover, when cleaning the unit of the DIY indoor water fountain, one should always make use of the soft material and fabric cloth to ensure that there are no such signs of wear and tear after the routine cleaning is conducted.  You should also take care of the cleaning material which helps you in maintaining the acrylic water walls in the correct and long lasting manner.",
